.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
.DS_Store
state/secrets.json
# Runtime data (briefs, designs, listings, escalations, usage, log, fabricated tools).
# All regenerable; nothing here is code worth tracking.
state/

# Harvested photographs of real businesses — Google review-platform images and
# Street View — keyed by record id. They are READ for information and never
# republished, which is a rule the code enforces on a built page and which this
# repository broke for months: 28 of them were tracked, for three named
# businesses, in a repository intended to go public. They are somebody else's
# copyright and somebody else's premises, and they are regenerable.
leads/

# Golden-test failure artifacts, written by `flutter test` when a comparison
# fails. Debris from a run, not source.
app/test/failures/

# Installed plugins. Each one is its own repository now, cloned in here — so
# this checkout can be public while the plugins stay private. Removing them
# from here does NOT remove them from this repository's history; making it
# public would still expose everything they once held.
plugins/

# Agent prompts, wherever they are not inside a plugin. A plugin's own
# repository tracks its prompts — keeping them out of version control as well
# as out of a public core meant they lived on one laptop, and a fresh clone
# booted with 42 missing files.
prompts/

# Vendored third-party skill data (3.6 MB of CSVs). Re-fetch with:
#   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill
#   cp -r ui-ux-pro-max-skill/.claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max .claude/skills/
.claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/

# Generated site output that lands at the repo root. Forge is scoped to a
# per-lead build directory, but an early run wrote here — and a spec site names
# a real business, so it must never be committed by accident.
/index.html
/styles.css

# Brand marks and their Krita sources. Kept out of the tree for the same
# reason as prompts/: the name and the mark are the part of this worth
# keeping private, and the .kra files are a working directory, not a build
# input. Nothing in the app reads from here — assets it needs are copied
# into the app's own tree and committed deliberately.
brand/

# Plugin prompts, for the same reason as `prompts/`: the text is the private
# part. The committed half is the `prompts=(...)` declaration in plugin.py.
plugins/*/prompts/
plugins/*/__pycache__/

# Flutter app build output
app/build/
app/.dart_tool/
app/linux/flutter/ephemeral/
app/android/.gradle/

# A plugin's personal data. `plugins/*/prompts/` above covers the prompt text;
# this covers the rest of what a plugin is given ABOUT a person rather than
# about the work. `job_hunt`'s profile holds a phone number, an address and a
# tax id, and it sits next to a committed `profile.example.yaml` that shows the
# shape — which is exactly the arrangement where the wrong one gets added.
plugins/*/profile/profile.yaml
plugins/*/profile/*.pdf
